@startuml ShoppingBasketSequenceDiagram

title Shopping Basket Pricing — Sequence Diagram
autonumber

actor User
participant "Console Program" as App
participant "Dependency Injection Container" as DI
participant "ShoppingBasketPricingService" as Pricing
participant "InMemoryProductCatalog" as Catalog
participant "QuantityOfferStrategy" as Quantity
participant "PercentageDiscountStrategy" as Percentage

== Startup ==
App -> DI: Register services with AddShoppingBasket()
App -> DI: Build provider and resolve IShoppingBasketPricingService
DI -> Pricing: Construct with catalog and offer strategies
DI --> App: Return pricing service

== Read and validate basket ==
App -> User: Prompt for product: quantity entries
User -> App: Enter basket text
App -> App: Split input into comma-separated entries

alt All entries are valid
	loop Each entry
		App -> App: Split at ':' and parse quantity
		App -> App: Validate product name and quantity > 0
		App -> App: Aggregate into case-insensitive dictionary
		note right of App
			Duplicate product names with different casing
			are combined. Accumulated quantity is overflow-checked.
		end note
	end

	== Calculate total ==
	App -> Pricing: CalculateTotalPence(quantities)
	Pricing -> Pricing: Validate, trim, and normalize product names

	loop Each normalized product
		Pricing -> Catalog: GetByName(productName)
		alt Product exists
			Catalog --> Pricing: Product (unit price and offers)
			Pricing -> Pricing: Calculate base line total

			loop Each offer in priority order
				alt Quantity bundle offer
					Pricing -> Quantity: Apply(offer, quantity, unit price, line total)
					Quantity --> Pricing: Adjusted line total
				else Percentage discount offer
					Pricing -> Percentage: Apply(offer, quantity, unit price, line total)
					Percentage --> Pricing: Adjusted line total
				end
				Pricing -> Pricing: Update line total
			end

			Pricing -> Pricing: Add line total to basket total
		else Product is unknown
			Catalog --> Pricing: Throw ArgumentException
			Pricing --> App: Propagate exception
			App -> User: Display error and set exit code 1
		end
	end

	Pricing -> Pricing: Round total and convert to integer pence
	Pricing --> App: Return total pence
	App -> User: Display total in pence and pounds
else Invalid format, blank name, nonpositive quantity, or overflow
	App -> App: Throw ArgumentException
	App -> User: Display validation error and set exit code 1
end

@enduml
